 ## Overview
-This method constructs the connectivity information for the quadrilateral mesh generated by Dual Marching Cubes, specifically storing vertices, faces, next halfedges, and twin edge relationships [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently linking halfedges across cell boundaries on the GPU by using a hash table to group halfedges by their incident vertex pairs, handling boundary and non-manifold edges in parallel [S1]. It differs from sibling methods by focusing exclusively on the global connectivity assembly phase after local geometry generation, whereas [Dual Marching Cubes Table Generation](2069-dual-marching-cubes-table-generation.md) handles lookup tables and [Manifold Dual Marching Cubes](2135-manifold-dual-marching-cubes.md) enforces manifold constraints during extraction.
+This method constructs the connectivity information for the quadrilateral mesh generated by Dual Marching Cubes, specifically storing vertices, faces, next halfedges, and twin edge relationships [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently linking halfedges across cell boundaries on the GPU by using a hash table to group halfedges by their incident vertex pairs, handling boundary and non-manifold edges in parallel [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-The construction is performed in two parallel GPU kernels. The first kernel computes local halfedge properties and inserts them into a hash table. The second kernel processes the hash table to establish global twin relationships.
-
